<article class="env-lemma" id="0ES9">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0ES9">Lemma <span data-tag="0ES9">82.30.3</span>.</a> In Situation <a href="/tag/0EDT" data-tag="0EDT">82.2.1</a> let $X/B$ be good. Suppose that $\mathcal{E}$ sits in an exact sequence </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  0 \to \mathcal{E}_1 \to \mathcal{E} \to \mathcal{E}_2 \to 0  \]
</div>
  <p> of finite locally free sheaves $\mathcal{E}_ i$ of rank $r_ i$. The total Chern classes satisfy </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  c(\mathcal{E}) = c(\mathcal{E}_1) c(\mathcal{E}_2)  \]
</div>
  <p> in $A^*(X)$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      The proof is identical to the proof of Chow Homology, Lemma <a href="/tag/02UI" data-tag="02UI">42.40.3</a> replacing the lemmas used there by Lemmas <a href="/tag/0ERS" data-tag="0ERS">82.26.9</a>, <a href="/tag/0ES8" data-tag="0ES8">82.30.2</a>, and <a href="/tag/0ERY" data-tag="0ERY">82.28.1</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>